Input: {"question": "Where is the Boston and Maine Railroad Depot located?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0350-a37f3dcd86f9:d00", "start": 0, "end": 163, "text": "Raymond Railroad Depot The Raymond Railroad Depot is a historic former Boston and Maine railroad station at 1 Depot Street in the center of Raymond, New Hampshire."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0350-a37f3dcd86f9:d00", "start": 164, "end": 251, "text": "Built in 1893, it is one of the state's finest and least-altered 19th-century stations."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0350-a37f3dcd86f9:d00", "start": 252, "end": 390, "text": "It is presently operated by the Raymond Historical Society as a museum, and was added to the National Register of Historic Places in 1979."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0350-a37f3dcd86f9:d00", "start": 391, "end": 599, "text": "The Raymond Railroad Depot is located in the town's village center, on the east side of Main Street between Depot Street and the former right-of-way of the Boston and Maine Railroad Portsmouth Branch, now the"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0350-a37f3dcd86f9:d01", "start": 0, "end": 161, "text": "Raymond Railroad Depot The Raymond Railroad Depot is a historic former Boston and Maine railroad station at 1 Depot Street in the center of Salem, Massachusetts."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0350-a37f3dcd86f9:d01", "start": 162, "end": 249, "text": "Built in 1893, it is one of the state's finest and least-altered 19th-century stations."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0350-a37f3dcd86f9:d01", "start": 250, "end": 388, "text": "It is presently operated by the Raymond Historical Society as a museum, and was added to the National Register of Historic Places in 1979."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0350-a37f3dcd86f9:d01", "start": 389, "end": 615, "text": "The Raymond Railroad Depot is located in the town's village center, on the east side of Main Street between Depot Street and the former right-of-way of the Boston and Maine Railroad Portsmouth Branch, now the Salem Rail Trail."}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0350-a37f3dcd86f9:d02", "start": 0, "end": 125, "text": "Stoneham Railroad Depot The Stoneham Railroad Depot is a historic train station at 36 Pine Street in Stoneham, Massachusetts."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0350-a37f3dcd86f9:d02", "start": 126, "end": 273, "text": "Built in 1895 by the Boston and Maine Railroad, it is one of two surviving train stations in the town, and the only one still at its original site."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0350-a37f3dcd86f9:d02", "start": 274, "end": 350, "text": "The building was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1984."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0350-a37f3dcd86f9:d02", "start": 351, "end": 390, "text": "It is now used for commercial purposes."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0350-a37f3dcd86f9:d02", "start": 391, "end": 513, "text": "The railroad depot is located two blocks east of its Central Square, at the northeast corner of Franklin and Pine Streets."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0350-a37f3dcd86f9:d02", "start": 514, "end": 582, "text": "It is a single-story brick building resting on a granite foundation,"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0350-a37f3dcd86f9:d03", "start": 0, "end": 181, "text": "built at the same time as the Concord and Claremont by the same builder, Joseph Barnard (and joining the latter just west of the Contoocook Depot), once had nearly identical depots."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0350-a37f3dcd86f9:d03", "start": 182, "end": 328, "text": "The destroyed station at Hillsborough Bridge, the original terminus of the Contoocook Valley Railroad, was a virtual twin to the Contoocook Depot."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0350-a37f3dcd86f9:d03", "start": 329, "end": 409, "text": "Like the Contoocook and Warner buildings, it measured twenty-four by fifty feet."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0350-a37f3dcd86f9:d03", "start": 410, "end": 517, "text": "Throughout the period from 1849 to 1960, the Contoocook Depot was the commercial hub of Contoocook Village."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0350-a37f3dcd86f9:d03", "start": 518, "end": 614, "text": "The building not only served as the point of arrival and departure for travelers to and from the"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0350-a37f3dcd86f9:d04", "start": 0, "end": 24, "text": "for making this happen ?"}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0350-a37f3dcd86f9:d04", "start": 25, "end": 151, "text": "Different fundraising methods are in place such as a custom-named brick for an apron between the depot and the Pullman coach ."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0350-a37f3dcd86f9:d04", "start": 152, "end": 343, "text": "Additional fundraising efforts include the Starry Starry Weekend - Christmas at the Depot artisan craft fair , mailers , gift shop and the reopening of the Contoocook Village Welcome Center ."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0350-a37f3dcd86f9:d04", "start": 344, "end": 402, "text": "What are the organization 's capabilities for doing this ?"}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0350-a37f3dcd86f9:d04", "start": 403, "end": 506, "text": "Our board of directors is a strong group with many local assets to accomplish our fundraising efforts ."}, "D5S6": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0350-a37f3dcd86f9:d04", "start": 507, "end": 596, "text": "Many volunteers and organizations work together to help us meet our goals by contributing"}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0350-a37f3dcd86f9:d00", "card_id": "ramdocs-0350-a37f3d